Task 3 - Create a Java snippet that checks if a user can book a movie ticket on BookMyShow: declare variables for userAge (int) and hasPaymentMethod (boolean). 
         Use logical and relational operators to print 'Booking allowed' only if the user is 18 or older and has a payment method linked.
Answer - 
        import java.util.Scanner;
        public class hello
        {
            public static void main(String[] args)
            {
                Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
                System.out.println("Welcome to Book My Show Application");
                System.out.println("Enter your Age");
                int age=sc.nextInt();
                System.out.println("Is Payment Method is linked");
                boolean payment = sc.nextBoolean();
                if(age>=18 && payment == true)
                {
                    System.out.println("Booking Allowed");
                }
                else
                {
                    System.out.println("Bookin Isn't Allowed");
                }
            }
        }
